  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which 1-Acetyl-3-Methoxycarbonyl-Beta-Carboline may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, through its interaction with Phosphodiesterase 6C. This compound appears to act as a target of multiple compounds, including 2,4,6-Trihydroxy-3-(3,3-Dimethylallyl)Acetophenone, (+)-Vouacapenic Acid, and 4,5-dihydro-2-methyl-3(2H)-furanone, all of which are known to target the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The shared target of these compounds at Phosphodiesterase 6C implies a common pathway or mechanism of action, possibly involving the inhibition of a key enzyme in the pathway that regulates the activity of the EZH2 complex. The scores from the paths are consistent, suggesting a plausible and well-supported relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between the compound and the EZH2 complex, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the specific mode of action and the biological relevance of this interaction.",
